+| `LIGHTNING-K05` | Verified / UE 5.8.1 | VibeUE scratch `ConnectPins`/`DisconnectPin` have NO `INPUT`/`OUTPUT` sentinel — node ids are GUIDs only (`FindNodeByGuid`); resolve the real Input/Output node ids via `ListNodes` (call with the module name) before wiring. All scratch modules created on one emitter share ONE scratch graph (Input/Output nodes are shared; ListNodes/ListConnections return the union). Driver scripts must check plain-boolean `result=false` as well as `result.bSuccess` — a missing sentinel wire fails silently otherwise. Symptom of a missing MapSet backbone wire: compile stays clean, but the written attribute never reaches the output map. |
+| `LIGHTNING-K06` | Verified / UE 5.8.1 | Editor-side Niagara reads (GetEmitterTopology/GetScriptStackTopology/GetEmitterInputValues/compile state) can all look healthy while the runtime emitter instance spawns zero particles — a corrupted runtime binding after many same-session structural edits. Decisive probe: `NiagaraToolset_Component.GetRuntimeState` in PIE. Fix: RemoveEmitter + AddEmitter (Minimal template), then re-attach scratch modules via AddModule(moduleAsset=existing pad script) and re-add renderers; CreateScratchModule after removal orphans the old pad and suffixed `_1` copies mislead later pin ops. |
