+| `LIGHTNING-K08` | Verified / UE 5.8.1 | `AddUserVariables` DefaultValue must be one FNiagaraExt_InstancedValue: `{struct={refPath}, value={...}}` with the inner struct fields (FNiagaraPosition is FVector3f `{x,y,z}`); split `defaultValue`/`value` keys fail JSON conversion. Position defaults read back as `{}` regardless of content, so verify functionally via runtime bounds. An early malformed-payload SetVariable once stored garbage Position overrides (fixed by an explicit-zero rewrite). Position-typed override variants exist in TWO payload sizes: canonical 24-byte FVector (editor UI / serialization, see GetCurrentParameterValue) and 12-byte FVector3f (toolset writes); SetOverrideParameterStoreValue accepts both. The stock `EnsureOverrideParametersConsistent` ensure (NiagaraComponent.cpp) memcmp'd sizeof(FVector)=24B against the variant buffer, overrunning 12-byte payloads — fixed engine-side to a size-aware comparison (IRIS-FIX marker, uncommitted in engine working tree; flow into the patch pipeline when convenient). |
